It is Saturday morning.
I am in our neighbourhood café.
I volunteer here every Saturday.
Today, on the weekend, there is a lot of rush.
Sunita is behind the counter.
She quickly prepares coffee and warm sandwiches.
I take it all to the customers.
"Maya, please take this coffee to the third table," Sunita says.
"Alright, I am taking it," saying this, I go.
I give the coffee and sandwich to the customer.
"Sir, your breakfast," I say.
"Thank you," the gentleman says with a smile.
Usually, only regular customers from our neighbourhood come here.
Today the café is very busy.
Many customers know me by name.
During a short break, Sunita and I chat.
"Maya, you are very skilled now," she says.
"That is all just because of your help," I say affectionately.
We smile again and welcome the new customers.
